COM            :  Common (Negative) terminal
V Ω →+ -||     :  Voltage, Resistance, Diode, Capacitance, Frequency, Continuity

============================================================
                 DIGITAL MULTIMETER ASCII SHEET
============================================================

 DIAL SYMBOLS:
   V==   : DC Voltage
   V~    : AC Voltage
   A==   : DC Current
   A~    : AC Current
   Ω     : Resistance
   )))   : Continuity (buzzer)
   →|+   : Diode Test
   -||-  : Capacitance
   Hz    : Frequency

============================================================
 VOLTAGE / CURRENT / RESISTANCE (OHM'S LAW)
============================================================
   V = I * R
   I = V / R
   R = V / I

   Use:
     V==  : measure DC rails, boards, sensors
     V~   : measure mains, AC outputs
     A==  : inline DC current
     A~   : clamp AC current
     Ω    : element, fuse, winding checks

============================================================
 POWER
============================================================
   P = V * I
   P = I^2 * R
   P = V^2 / R

   Field use:
     Heating elements, motors, load verification

============================================================
 AC / TRUE-RMS
============================================================
   VRMS = sqrt( (1/T) * ∫ v(t)^2 dt )
   Vpeak = VRMS * sqrt(2)
   Vpp   = 2 * Vpeak

   Notes:
     120 VRMS → ~170 Vpeak
     True-RMS required for non-sine loads

============================================================
 RESISTANCE & CONTINUITY
============================================================
   Continuity beeps when:
     R < R_threshold   (typically 30–50 Ω)

   Notes:
     Beep ≠ good load
     Elements can beep but still be weak/open under power

============================================================
 DIODE TEST
============================================================
   Forward drop:
     VF ≈ 0.6–0.7 V (silicon)

   Meter applies small current and reads drop.

============================================================
 CAPACITANCE
============================================================
   XC = 1 / (2π f C)
   E  = (1/2) * C * V^2

   Notes:
     Higher XC = weaker run cap
     Capacitance mode uses low-frequency test pulses

============================================================
 FREQUENCY
============================================================
   f = 1 / T
   T = 1 / f

   Use:
     Board PWM, inverter outputs, tach signals

============================================================
 FIELD TEST QUICK VALUES
============================================================
   Heating element: 8–12 Ω typical (dryer)
   Thermal fuse: 0 Ω (open = bad)
   High-limit: 0 Ω (open = tripped)
   Motor windings: low Ω but not zero
   Diode: 0.6–0.7 V forward, OL reverse
   Run cap: within ±5–10% of rating

============================================================
 SAFETY ASCII
============================================================
   ONE-HAND RULE:
     Keep one hand behind back when probing mains.

   PROBE ASCII:
     [RED +] → hot/positive
     [BLK -] → neutral/ground/common

